          "guid": "mtqgbayjas63gfm4",
          "message": {
            "text": "Document-root observation spans both sides of the lifecycle transition without changing target execution semantics. Blink revision 7d859f271c notifies mutation observers during child removal before disconnection in external/chromium/thirdparty/blink/renderer/core/dom/containernode.cc; the observer therefore captures insertion/removal while the linked executor keeps exact authored targeting.",
            "markdown": "Document-root observation spans both sides of the lifecycle transition without changing target execution semantics. Blink revision 7d859f271c notifies mutation observers during child removal before disconnection in external/chromium/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/container_node.cc; the observer therefore captures insertion/removal while the linked executor keeps exact authored targeting."
          },
          "locations": [
            {
              "physicalLocation": {
                "artifactLocation": {
                  "uri": "src/studio/interaction-observer.ts"
                },
                "region": {
                  "startLine": 511,
                  "endLine": 521,
                  "snippet": {
                    "text": "  const observesAttachmentLifecycle = event.kind === \"waitForState\" && (event.state === \"attached\" || event.state === \"detached\");\n  let target = page.locator(\"html\");\n  if (\"target\" in event && event.target != null) {\n    const resolved = await resolveStudioSemanticTarget(page, event.target, `${step.path}.target`, event.id, {\n      allowMissing: observesAttachmentLifecycle,\n    });\n    // An attachment wait cannot anchor observation to the target: it may not\n    // exist yet, and a detached target may disappear during the action. The\n    // document root keeps both lifecycle transitions inside one observer while\n    // the executor retains the authored locator and its strict cardinality.\n    if (!observesAttachmentLifecycle) target = resolved;"
                  }
                }
              }
            }
